# Normalise line endings to LF in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Prettier writes LF (its `endOfLine` default), while a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true produces CRLF — so `prettier --check` and eslint's prettier rule
# reported thousands of "Delete `␍`" errors on files nobody had touched, which is a large
# part of why formatting was treated as unfixable here. Pinning eol=lf makes the checkout
# match what the formatter produces on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
